-- title:
--   Branch ideals at a crossing intersect in (q)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $q$ with $N_0 \neq 0$, $q$ prime and $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, that is, the package of data and axioms (properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of the structure morphism, normality on affine opens, the identification of the generic geometric fibre with a curve model of the level-$N_0q$ modular function field together with its Galois and $q$-expansion compatibilities, smoothness and geometric integrality in characteristic $0$, and the sections $\varepsilon_\infty$, $\varepsilon_0$ and further data) for the Deligne–Rapoport model over $R_q$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 1$, and let $x = \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{crossingPt}\ \rho_O\ \mathrm{to}\kappa\ n$ be its image in $X_O = \mathfrak{X} \times_{R_q} \operatorname{Spec} O$ under `pullback.fst` followed by the zeroth component map and the base-change map `DRLevel.bcMap`. Assume the two points $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_\infty$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_0$ (for $\rho_O$, $\mathrm{to}\kappa$) both specialise to $x$, via `hinf` and `hzero`. Then, inside the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X_O,x}$, the intersection of the two ideals $\mathrm{comap}$ of the maximal ideals of the stalks at $\xi_\infty$ and at $\xi_0$ along the specialisation maps (the ideals $\mathrm{branchIdeal}$ of germs vanishing at the respective point) equals the principal ideal generated by the germ at $x$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained by pulling back $q \in O$ along the structure morphism $X_O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic form of the statement that near a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ the fibre is exactly the union of its two branches: the uniformiser $q$ generates the intersection of the two branch primes. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal) and by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart), which produce local coordinates at a crossing.
